CH = dict(num=13, tag="Grammar · Syllabus Topic 13",
 title="Reported Speech (Direct and Indirect Narration)",
 intro="Reported speech lets us tell what someone said without using their exact words. It tests four skills at once: choosing the reporting verb and the linking word, backshifting the tense, changing pronouns, and changing words of time and place. In the board exam it appears as a conversation or comic strip you must convert into a paragraph.",
 blocks=[
 ("h2", "Direct and Indirect Speech"),
 ("table", ["", "Direct speech", "Reported (indirect) speech"], [
  ["Meaning", "actual words of the speaker are quoted", "the idea is reported in the reporter's words"],
  ["Punctuation", "inverted commas and a comma / colon", "no inverted commas; full stop at the end"],
  ["Example", "He said to me, \"How are you?\"", "He asked me how I was."]]),
 ("p", "Two parts: the **reporting verb** (said to me, asked, told) in the reporting clause and the **reported speech** (the words spoken)."),
 ("h3", "Five steps in converting direct to reported speech"),
 ("steps", [("Step 1 — Change the reporting verb", "according to the kind of sentence: said / told (statement), asked / enquired (question), ordered / requested / advised (imperative), exclaimed (exclamation)."), ("Step 2 — Remove the comma and inverted commas", "and insert the right linking word: that, if / whether, a wh-word, to / not to."), ("Step 3 — Change the tense of the verb", "if the reporting verb is in the past (backshift); no change if it is present or future."), ("Step 4 — Change the pronouns", "I-person with the speaker (subject of the reporting verb), II-person with the listener (object), III-person no change."), ("Step 5 — Change words of time and place", "and end with a full stop (never a question mark or exclamation mark).")]),
 ("h2", "Changing the Reporting Verb and the Link Word"),
 ("table", ["Type of sentence", "Reporting verb: said to becomes", "Link word", "Example"], [
  ["Declarative (statement)", "told / said (to), informed, replied, added, explained", "that", "He said, \"I am tired.\" - He said that he was tired."],
  ["Interrogative, yes/no", "asked / enquired", "if / whether", "She said, \"Do you know him?\" - She asked if I knew him."],
  ["Interrogative, wh-", "asked", "the same wh-word", "He said, \"Where do you live?\" - He asked where I lived."],
  ["Imperative, affirmative", "ordered / told / requested / advised / urged / begged", "to", "He said, \"Go home.\" - He ordered me to go home."],
  ["Imperative, negative (Do not)", "forbade / advised / told", "not to", "He said, \"Do not run.\" - He told me not to run."],
  ["Exclamatory", "exclaimed (with joy / sorrow / surprise) / cried out", "that (+ strong word)", "She said, \"What a lovely day!\" - She exclaimed that it was a very lovely day."],
  ["Optative (wish, prayer)", "wished / prayed", "that / for", "He said, \"May you succeed!\" - He wished that I might succeed."],
  ["Assertive with 'Let' (suggestion)", "suggested / proposed", "that ... should", "He said, \"Let us go.\" - He suggested that we should go."]]),
 ("h2", "The Tense Change (Backshift)"),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "If the reporting verb is in the **present or future** (He says, He will say, He has said) the tense of the reported speech does **not** change. If the reporting verb is **past** (said, asked, told), the verb of the reported speech moves one step back."),
 ("table", ["Direct speech", "Reported speech", "Example"], [
  ["Present simple (do / does)", "Past simple", "\"I like tea.\" - He said that he liked tea."],
  ["Present continuous (is / am / are + -ing)", "Past continuous (was / were + -ing)", "\"I am reading.\" - She said that she was reading."],
  ["Present perfect (has / have + V3)", "Past perfect (had + V3)", "\"I have finished.\" - He said that he had finished."],
  ["Present perfect continuous", "Past perfect continuous", "\"I have been working.\" - He said that he had been working."],
  ["Past simple (V2)", "Past perfect (had + V3)", "\"I saw him.\" - She said that she had seen him."],
  ["Past continuous", "Past perfect continuous", "\"I was sleeping.\" - He said that he had been sleeping."],
  ["Past perfect", "no change (past perfect)", "\"I had left.\" - He said that he had left."],
  ["will / shall", "would", "\"I will go.\" - He said that he would go."],
  ["can", "could", "\"I can swim.\" - He said that he could swim."],
  ["may", "might", "\"I may come.\" - She said that she might come."],
  ["must", "must / had to", "\"I must go.\" - He said that he had to go."],
  ["would, could, should, might, ought to", "no change", "\"I should go.\" - He said that he should go."]]),
 ("h3", "When the tense does NOT change even if the reporting verb is in the past"),
 ("ul", ["**Universal truths and scientific facts:** *The teacher said, \"The earth moves round the sun.\" - The teacher said that the earth moves round the sun.*", "**Habits that still continue** and statements that are still true: *He said, \"I live in Jaipur.\" - He said that he lives in Jaipur* (if he still does).", "**Historical facts:** *He said that Akbar was born in 1542.*", "**Past perfect** and the modals would, could, should, might, ought to, used to.", "**Conditional (second / third)** and wishes: *If I were rich ... remains.*", "**Reported soon after speaking** (the same day, same situation): present tense may be kept."]),
 ("h2", "The Pronoun Rules"),
 ("table", ["Person in direct speech", "Changes to match", "Example"], [
  ["I person: I, me, my, we, us, our", "the subject (speaker) of the reporting verb", "Ram said, \"I like my school.\" - Ram said that he liked his school."],
  ["II person: you, your", "the object (listener) of the reporting verb", "Ram said to Sita, \"You are my friend.\" - Ram told Sita that she was his friend."],
  ["III person: he, she, it, they, him, them", "no change", "Ram said, \"She is late.\" - Ram said that she was late."]]),
 ("p", "If there is no object after the reporting verb, ask whom 'you' refers to: *He said, \"You are late.\"* - *He said that I was late* (if speaking to the reporter) or *that they were late* (if the listener is a group)."),
 ("p", "Note: (**I** - subject, **me** - object, **my** - possessive); change case along with person: *Ravi said to me, \"You helped me.\" - Ravi told me that I had helped him.*"),
 ("h2", "Words of Time and Place"),
 ("table", ["Direct speech", "Indirect speech (reporting verb in past)"], [
  ["now", "then"], ["today", "that day"], ["tonight", "that night"], ["yesterday", "the day before / the previous day"], ["tomorrow", "the next day / the following day"], ["last night / week / year", "the previous night / week / year"], ["next week / year", "the following week / year"], ["ago", "before"], ["here", "there"], ["this / these", "that / those"], ["thus / hence", "so / thence"], ["come", "go (if direction changes)"], ["the day before yesterday", "two days before"], ["the day after tomorrow", "in two days' time"]]),
 ("note", "REMEMBER", "These words change **only** if the time or place of the report differs from that of the original speech. In exam answers apply the table unless the question says otherwise."),
 ("h2", "Reporting Statements"),
 ("ul", ["*She said, \"I am very happy.\"* - She said that she was very happy.", "*He said to me, \"I will help you.\"* - He told me that he would help me. (said to + object becomes told)", "*Mother said, \"I have prepared the food.\"* - Mother said that she had prepared the food.", "*The teacher said to us, \"You must work hard.\"* - The teacher told us that we must / had to work hard.", "*Rita said, \"My brother came here yesterday.\"* - Rita said that her brother had gone there the day before."]),
 ("p", "**Say** is used when there is no listener mentioned; **tell** needs an object (*told me*); never 'said me'."),
 ("h2", "Reporting Questions"),
 ("h3", "Yes / No type (if, whether)"),
 ("ul", ["*He said to me, \"Are you ill?\"* - He asked me if / whether I was ill.", "*She said, \"Did you see the film?\"* - She asked if I had seen the film.", "*\"Can you swim?\" asked the coach.* - The coach asked if I could swim.", "Use **whether** when there is an alternative: *He asked whether I wanted tea or coffee.*"]),
 ("h3", "Wh- type (the wh-word is retained)"),
 ("ul", ["*He said, \"Where are you going?\"* - He asked me where I was going.", "*Mother said to me, \"What are you doing?\"* - Mother asked me what I was doing.", "*She said, \"Why did you come late?\"* - She asked why I had come late."]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "In reported questions the word order is **statement order** (subject before verb), there is no question mark, and no do / does / did: *He asked where I lived* (not 'where did I live'; not 'where I live?')."),
 ("h2", "Reporting Commands, Requests and Advice"),
 ("table", ["Direct", "Reported"], [
  ["He said to me, \"Go home.\"", "He ordered me to go home."],
  ["She said to him, \"Please help me.\"", "She requested him to help her."],
  ["The doctor said to him, \"Take rest.\"", "The doctor advised him to take rest."],
  ["The teacher said, \"Do not make a noise.\"", "The teacher told them not to make a noise."],
  ["The officer said to the soldiers, \"Fire!\"", "The officer ordered the soldiers to fire."],
  ["He said, \"Please let me go.\"", "He begged / requested to be allowed to go."],
  ["He said, \"Let us go for a walk.\"", "He suggested that we should go for a walk."]]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "Choose the reporting verb by sense: **order / command** (authority), **request** (please, kindly), **advise** (should, better), **warn** (be careful), **forbid** (negative commands), **beg** (strong request), **suggest** (let us)."),
 ("h2", "Reporting Exclamations and Wishes"),
 ("ul", ["*She said, \"Hurrah! We have won.\"* - She exclaimed with joy that they had won.", "*He said, \"Alas! I am ruined.\"* - He exclaimed with sorrow that he was ruined.", "*She said, \"What a lovely day!\"* - She exclaimed that it was a very lovely day.", "*The teacher said, \"Bravo! You have done well.\"* - The teacher applauded him saying that he had done well.", "*He said, \"May you live long!\"* - He prayed that I might live long.", "*\"Good morning,\" he said.* - He wished me good morning. *\"Happy birthday!\"* - He wished her a happy birthday."]),
 ("p", "Words like Oh!, Alas!, Hurrah!, Wow! are dropped and expressed by the reporting verb (exclaimed with joy / sorrow / surprise / grief / wonder)."),
 ("h2", "Mixed Sentences"),
 ("p", "When one direct speech contains two or more kinds of sentences, convert each separately with its own link word and keep the reporting verb for each: *He said, \"I am tired. Will you make some tea?\"* - He said that he was tired and asked me if I would make some tea."),
 ("ul", ["Two statements: join with **and** / **that**.", "Statement + question: *said that ... and asked ...*", "Question + command: *asked ... and told / requested ...*", "Commas, full stops inside the quote mark the breaks."]),
 ("p", "Longer extract: *The teacher said, \"Good morning, children. Open your books. Who will read the first paragraph?\"* - The teacher wished the children good morning, told them to open their books and asked who would read the first paragraph."),
 ("h2", "Special Cases"),
 ("h3", "A. Sentences with 'let'"),
 ("p", "*Let us go* - suggestion: *He suggested that we should go.* *Let him go* - permission / order: *He ordered that he should be allowed to go.* *Let there be light* - *He said that there should be light.*"),
 ("h3", "B. Sentences with 'should, ought to, must'"),
 ("p", "No change in should, ought to, would, could, might. 'Must' is unchanged or becomes 'had to' for obligation; remains 'must' for certainty or prohibition: *He said, \"You must not smoke.\" - He said that I must not smoke / He told me not to smoke.*"),
 ("h3", "C. Conditionals"),
 ("p", "*She said, \"If I were rich, I would buy a car.\"* - She said that if she were rich, she would buy a car. (no change). *He said, \"If it rains, I will stay.\"* - He said that if it rained, he would stay."),
 ("h3", "D. Questions with 'shall I / shall we'"),
 ("p", "Offer: *He said, \"Shall I help you?\"* - He offered to help me. Suggestion: *\"Shall we go?\"* - He suggested going / asked if we should go."),
 ("h3", "E. 'Yes' and 'No' answers"),
 ("p", "*\"Do you like it?\" - \"Yes.\"* - He said that he did. *She said, \"No, I can't.\"* - She replied in the negative / said that she couldn't."),
 ("h3", "F. Greetings and thanks"),
 ("p", "*\"Thank you,\" he said to me.* - He thanked me. *\"Congratulations!\"* - He congratulated me. *\"Sorry!\"* - He apologised."),
 ("h2", "Reporting Verbs and Their Patterns"),
 ("table", ["Pattern", "Verbs", "Example"], [
  ["verb + that-clause", "say, tell, state, explain, announce, claim, argue, complain, admit, deny, promise, add, remark", "He admitted that he had made a mistake."],
  ["verb + object + to-infinitive", "order, tell, advise, ask, request, warn, invite, remind, urge, encourage, permit, instruct", "She advised him to rest."],
  ["verb + to-infinitive", "offer, refuse, promise, agree, threaten, demand", "He refused to help."],
  ["verb + gerund / preposition", "suggest, deny, admit, insist on, apologise for, accuse of, thank for, congratulate on", "She apologised for being late."],
  ["verb + object + preposition + gerund", "accuse, blame, thank, congratulate, warn against, prevent from", "He accused me of lying."],
  ["verb + wh-/if clause", "ask, wonder, enquire, want to know", "He wondered whether she would come."]]),
 ("p", "Better reporting verbs make better answers: instead of 'said that he was sorry' write *apologised*; instead of 'said that he would help' write *promised to help*."),
 ("h2", "Dialogue to Paragraph and Comic-Strip Tasks"),
 ("p", "Board papers give a short conversation (sometimes a comic strip) and a paragraph with blanks, e.g. 'Rama told Sita (a) ____ ...'. Fill the blanks with indirect speech. Method:"),
 ("steps", [("Step 1 — Identify the speaker and listener", "for each line; the speaker of the line before the blank is the subject of the reporting verb."), ("Step 2 — Decide the sentence type", "statement, question, command or exclamation, and the reporting verb already given in the paragraph (told, asked, suggested, exclaimed)."), ("Step 3 — Backshift", "tense, pronouns, time and place words; check that the blank follows the linking word in the paragraph."), ("Step 4 — Read the whole paragraph aloud", "for flow and for the correct word order.")]),
 ("h3", "Worked example (from the syllabus pattern)"),
 ("p", "Rama: I am going to the jungle. / Sita: Why? / Rama: I have been banished for fourteen years by my father. / Sita: Oh! It is very sad. Can I go with you? / Rama: No. Stay at home to take care of my old parents."),
 ("p", "Rama told Sita (a) **that he was going to the jungle**. She asked him (b) **why he was going to the jungle** (c) Rama said **that he had been banished for fourteen years by his father**. Sita exclaimed that it was very sad and asked Rama (d) **if she could go with him**. Rama told her not to go and asked her to stay at home to take care of his old parents."),
 ("h3", "Notes-to-report tasks"),
 ("p", "Sometimes notes of a speech are given. Use passive-like reporting verbs: *The speaker said that ..., added that ..., pointed out that ..., concluded by saying that ...*"),
 ("h2", "Common Errors"),
 ("table", ["Wrong", "Right", "Reason"], [
  ["He said me that he was ill.", "He told me that he was ill.", "said needs no object; told does"],
  ["She asked where was I going.", "She asked where I was going.", "statement order"],
  ["He asked if did I like it.", "He asked if I liked it.", "no do/did"],
  ["He said that he will come tomorrow.", "He said that he would come the next day.", "tense and time word"],
  ["He told to me to go.", "He told me to go.", "no 'to' before the object"],
  ["She asked that what was my name.", "She asked what my name was.", "no 'that' with wh-word"],
  ["He said that the earth moved round the sun.", "He said that the earth moves round the sun.", "universal truth"],
  ["He suggested me to go.", "He suggested that I should go.", "suggest takes that-clause / gerund"],
  ["She asked me where do I live?", "She asked me where I lived.", "no question mark, no inversion"]]),
 ("h2", "Quick Check"),
 ("qa", [
  ("Report: He said, \"I am busy now.\"", "He said that he was busy then."),
  ("Report: She said to him, \"Where do you live?\"", "She asked him where he lived."),
  ("Report: The mother said to her son, \"Don't go out.\"", "The mother told her son not to go out."),
  ("Report: He said, \"I have finished my work.\"", "He said that he had finished his work."),
  ("Report: The teacher said, \"Honesty is the best policy.\"", "The teacher said that honesty is the best policy."),
  ("Report: \"What a beautiful scene!\" said Ravi.", "Ravi exclaimed that it was a very beautiful scene."),
  ("Report: Mohan said, \"Shall I carry your bag?\"", "Mohan offered to carry my bag."),
  ("Which is correct: He asked me what was I doing / what I was doing?", "what I was doing")])
 ],
 takeaways=[
 "Link words: that (statement), if / whether (yes/no), same wh-word (wh-question), to / not to (commands).",
 "Reporting verb present/future: no tense change. Past: backshift present-past, past-past perfect, will-would, can-could, may-might.",
 "No change for universal truths, past perfect, would/could/should/might/ought to.",
 "I-person follows the subject, II-person follows the object, III-person unchanged.",
 "Now-then, today-that day, tomorrow-the next day, yesterday-the day before, here-there, this-that.",
 "Questions become statements: statement order, no question mark, no do/did.",
 "Choose precise reporting verbs: order, request, advise, warn, forbid, suggest, exclaim, promise, apologise."
 ])
